<reference id="_Toc235450430" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Inline equation</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a &lt;math&gt; element placed inline within a &lt;p&gt; element alongside surrounding text.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>equation</keyword>
        <keyword>inline</keyword>
        <keyword>within</keyword>
        <keyword>MathML</keyword>
        <keyword>Inline</keyword>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>equation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>inline</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
     <section>
     <p>Consider a <codeph>&lt;math&gt;</codeph> element placed inline within a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element alongside surrounding text.</p>
       <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <title>Inline equation within text</title>
         <tgroup cols="2">
           <colspec colname="c1"/>
           <colspec colname="c2"/>
           <thead>
             <row>
               <entry>
                 <b>HTML Input</b>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                 <b>DITA Output</b>
               </entry>
             </row>
           </thead>
           <tbody>
             <row>
               <entry>
                 <codeblock>
&lt;p>
  The formula
  &lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
    &lt;mrow>
      &lt;mi>E&lt;/mi>
      &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
      &lt;mi>m&lt;/mi>
      &lt;msup>
        &lt;mi>c&lt;/mi>
        &lt;mn>2&lt;/mn>
      &lt;/msup>
    &lt;/mrow>
  &lt;/math>
  defines energy equivalence.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                 <codeblock>
&lt;p>
  The formula
  &lt;equation-inline>
    &lt;mathml>
      &lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
        &lt;mrow>
          &lt;mi>E&lt;/mi>
          &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
          &lt;mi>m&lt;/mi>
          &lt;msup>
            &lt;mi>c&lt;/mi>
            &lt;mn>2&lt;/mn>
          &lt;/msup>
        &lt;/mrow>
      &lt;/math>
    &lt;/mathml>
  &lt;/equation-inline>
  defines energy equivalence.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
               </entry>
             </row>
           </tbody>
         </tgroup>
       </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter detects the <codeph>&lt;math&gt;</codeph> element positioned inline within a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element and preserves the MathML content inline within the surrounding <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element. No <codeph>&lt;equation-block&gt;</codeph> wrapper is produced for inline equations.</p>
<note type="note"> The generated MathML structure is preserved from the HTML source. Validate mathematical output after conversion to ensure rendering accuracy in HTML, PDF, and downstream publishing systems.</note>
       </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
